Change:
- `SloObservationOutboxDelivery` reads one record/value-byte bounded page and, for each item, durably merges into `PersistentSloObservationCollector` before deleting the exact source record by its digest.
- Collector admission or persistence failure propagates and leaves that observation in the durable Shard outbox. A crash after collector persistence but before source deletion leaves the record available for idempotent replay.
- The adapter is a local delivery seam for a future exporter worker. It does not add an async worker/queue, ordinary metric exporter, gap accounting, certification mode, production authorization, or production assembly.
- The RocksDB regression writes a Start to the outbox, persists its collector merge, opens a second collector on the same state file, then delivers the source record and checks the projection, exact outbox deletion, and empty follow-up page. This simulates the persisted crash window by same-JVM state-file reopen; it is not a process-kill test. A capacity-rejection regression verifies the source remains while the collector has no observation.

